Q: How to make Ctrl+C always quit a while loop in Bash properly? A: <pre><code>#!/bin/bash

function close {
  pkill -9 -P $PID
}
trap close SIGINT SIGABRT SIGTERM

function myfoo {
   foo bar &amp;
   PID=$!
   wait $PID
   return $?
}

func() {
 while myfoo ; do
   : 
 done
}
</code></pre>
<p><code>foo bar</code> is sent in background so that the script can exit when ctrl+c is pressed.</p>
